.\" man/man3/Docv::Config.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Config" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Config \- The user configuration in \fB\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini\fR (\fB\%\(ti/.config/docv/config.ini\fR when the variable is unset or not an absolute path).
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Config\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The user configuration in \fB\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini\fR
(\fB\%\(ti/.config/docv/config.ini\fR when the variable is unset or not an
absolute path). \fB\%Config.load\fR writes a commented default file when none
exists.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBBOOLEANS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BOOLEANS = {
  "true" => true,
  "yes" => true,
  "on" => true,
  "1" => true,
  "false" => false,
  "no" => false,
  "off" => false,
  "0" => false,
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Words accepted for boolean values.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBCOLORS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
COLORS = "[colors]\en; Styles of the viewer, one per role. A style is attribute words (bold,\en; italic, underline, reverse, dim), a foreground color, and \e"on\e" with a\en; background color: \e"bold cyan\e", \e"black on yellow\e", \e"on background+12\e".\en; Colors: default, foreground, background, black, red, green, yellow,\en; blue, magenta, cyan, white (bright\-black ... bright\-white for 8\-15), a\en; palette number 0\-255 or #rrggbb. Named and numbered colors are the\en; terminal theme\(aqs own; +N or \-N ramps a color N percent toward the\en; theme\(aqs foreground or background. With NO_COLOR set, colors are off\en; and these are ignored. Uncomment a line to change a role.\en"
.EE
.RE
.PP
The \fB\%[colors]\fR explanation in \fB\%DEFAULT\fR, followed there by every role
with its default, commented out.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBDEFAULT\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
DEFAULT = String.build do |io|
  ((((io << ROFF) << \(aq\en\(aq) << VIEWER) << \(aq\en\(aq) << COLORS
  Theme::DEFAULT.each do |role, spec| ((((io << "; ") << (Theme.key(role))) << " = ") << spec) << \(aq\en\(aq end
end
.EE
.RE
.PP
The file written when no configuration exists.
.RE
.PP
\fBFILE = "config.ini"\fR
.TP 4
\fBKEYS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
KEYS = {
  "roff" => Set {"unsafe"},
  "viewer" => Set {"start\-wrapped", "syntax\-highlighting", "dock", "dock\-width", "dock\-open", "search\-threads"},
  "colors" => Theme::KEYS.keys.to_set,
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Known keys per section.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBRANGES = {"dock\-width" => 16..400, "search\-threads" => 0..1024}\fR
Allowed ranges of the integer keys.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.load(path : String = self.path, create : Bool = true) : Config\fR
Reads the configuration at \fIpath\fR. When the file does not exist it is
created with \fB\%DEFAULT\fR if \fIcreate\fR is set, and the defaults apply.
.PP
\fBdef self.new(path : String | Nil = nil, unsafe : Bool = false, colors : Hash(Docv::Theme::Role, Docv::Theme::Spec) = {} of Theme::Role => Theme::Spec, start_wrapped : Bool = true, syntax_highlighting : Bool = true, viewer : ViewerSettings = ViewerSettings.new)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse(text : String, path : String | Nil = nil) : Config\fR
Parses configuration \fItext\fR.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.directory : String\fR
The configuration directory: \fB\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.path : String\fR
The configuration file path.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef colors : Hash(Theme::Role, Theme::Spec)\fR
Role styles from \fB\%[colors]\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef options(stdin : IO | Nil = nil) : Options\fR
Parsing options from this configuration; \fIstdin\fR feeds \fB\%.rd\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef path : String | Nil\fR
The file this configuration was read from, if any.
.TP 4
\fBdef start_wrapped? : Bool\fR
Whether the viewer starts in the wrapped layout.
.TP 4
\fBdef syntax_highlighting? : Bool\fR
Whether code examples are syntax highlighted.
.TP 4
\fBdef theme : Theme\fR
The viewer theme: the defaults with the \fB\%[colors]\fR overrides.
.TP 4
\fBdef unsafe? : Bool\fR
Whether unsafe roff requests run.
.TP 4
\fBdef viewer : ViewerSettings\fR
The dock and search settings of the viewer.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/config.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Config::Error" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
